{{was wotd|2015|January|19}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|acertener}}, from ({{m|fro|a-||to, towards}} + {{m|fro|certener||make sure of}}, from the adjective {{m|fro|certain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/æsəˈteɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ăs-ər-tānʹ}}, {{IPA|/æsɚˈteɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-ascertain.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪn|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|as|cer|tain|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[find out]] [[definitely]]; to [[discover]] or [[establish]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1905|author=[[w:Emma Orczy|Baroness Emmuska Orczy]]
|title=[[w:The Case of Miss Elliott|The Tremarn Case]]
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL8479084W
|passage=“There the cause of death was soon '''ascertained''' ; the victim of this daring outrage had been stabbed to death from ear to ear with a long, sharp instrument, in shape like an antique stiletto, which […] was subsequently found under the cushions of the hansom.&nbsp;[…]”}}
#: ''As soon as we '''ascertain''' what the situation is, we can plan how to proceed.''

